Extend the Wi-Fi variants' local trusted-LAN root page with a
small "Recent logs" viewer on top of accepted GET /api/logs
from patch 0013. Applied only to nanoc6-wifi and
atoms3-lite-wifi via variants.json; nanoc6-thread never
applies, compiles, links, or serves it.

Scope, kept minimal (no polling, no WebSocket, no OTA, no
authentication, no API changes, no log-capture changes, no
settings changes):

  * MODIFY main/aliro_local_web.cpp: extend kIndexHtml with a
    Recent logs section:
      - <h2>Recent logs</h2>
      - <button id="logs-refresh">Refresh logs</button>
      - direct <a href="/api/logs"> link
      - bounded-height <pre id="logs"> (max-height 20rem, scrolls;
        pre-wrap; word-break; monospace)
      - separate <p id="logs-status" role="status" aria-live=
        "polite"> for success and errors
    A new <script> IIFE, SEPARATE from the QR IIFE and the
    settings IIFE, fetches /api/logs once on load and on every
    click of #logs-refresh. It requires response.ok, reads
    response.text() (letting r.text() reject with its original
    error name so the outer catch classifies network/body
    failures correctly), and assigns the unredacted result to
    #logs via textContent. Any '<script>' or HTML in the log
    body is therefore rendered as literal text and never
    evaluated. A failed refresh only updates #logs-status —
    the last successful log snapshot in #logs is preserved.
    /api/logs is added to the machine-endpoint list.

Explicit non-goals for this patch: no settings backend change,
no log-capture change (patch 0013 unchanged), no polling, no
WebSocket, no OTA, no authentication, no cJSON or new runtime
dependency, no external asset, no partition change.

